    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0416" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 (D) Regulations/3275: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-07-16T18:00:00-04:00">July 16, 1941—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>352. For Boal from Feis. Please confirm by telegraph the Department’s
                    understanding that Douglas’ letter to Wiechers<anchor n="45" xml:id="d330-f1"/>
                    is dated July 15, 1941 and that the decree establishing export control was
                    actually signed on July 10 and published on July 15<anchor n="46"
                        xml:id="d330-f2"/> in the form transmitted to the Department in your 301 of
                    July 11, 3 p.m. [Feis.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d330-f1" n="45" xml:id="d330-f1-content">
                <p>Luciano Wiechers, economic adviser of the Bank of Mexico, and Mexican
                    representative in the export control discussions.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d330-f2" n="46" xml:id="d330-f2-content">
                <p>On July 18 the Department received confirmation of its understanding. The decree
                    and letter, which constitute agreement, were published in the newspaper <hi
                        rendition="#italic">El Nacional</hi> on July 15, 1941.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
